------ Employee Management CRUD Application ------

Database    : company_db
Table       : employee
        id              int PK, auto increment
        name            varchar(100)
        place           varchar(100)
        mobile          varchar(15) unique
        email           varchar(100)
        department      varchar(100)
        salary          int
        joining_date    date

------> Requirements

Create a class named EmployeeManager

1. Connect to Database
Establish a connection to the MySQL database company_db.

2. Add Record
Accept all employee field values.
Insert the employee record into the employee table.
Display: "Employee Added Successfully."

3. View All Records
Fetch and display all employee records from the table.

4. Update Record
Accept the employee id.
Update the required employee details.
Display: "Employee Updated Successfully."

5. Delete Record
Accept the employee id.
Delete the corresponding employee record.
Display: "Employee Deleted Successfully."

Note: Implement all database operations as methods inside the EmployeeManager class.